text:
sara kim: Heads-up — integrating the new next-starter-with-llama into the quickplay repo and hitting weird auth behavior on Edge runtimes.
evan: I ran into this during a demo. The sample's helper uses the sdk-edge fetch wrapper and sometimes the retry loses the Authorization header, causing repeated 401s.
priya: quick debug: sdk-js and sdk-edge differ in how they clone requests for retry. sdk-js copies headers; sdk-edge does a new Request(origReq) which on some runtimes drops ephemeral headers.
sara kim: can we add an explicit header merge in the sample helper to be defensive? new users copy the helper and get stuck.
evan: suggested workaround snippet for README and sample helper:
```js
// defensive auth helper
export async function sampleFetch(input, init = {}) {
  const orig = input instanceof Request ? input : new Request(input, init);
  const headers = new Headers(orig.headers);
  if (process.env.SAMPLE_TOKEN) headers.set('authorization', `Bearer ${process.env.SAMPLE_TOKEN}`);
  return fetch(new Request(orig.url, { method: orig.method, headers, body: await orig.clone().arrayBuffer() }));
}
```
priya: I'll add a tiny e2e that simulates token expiry and asserts we don't spin retries forever. will add to samples-ci.
build-bot: CI job samples/e2e scheduled for branch fix/sample-auth-merge.
sara kim: thanks — also adding a one-line note to onboarding doc: "If Edge templates hit repeated 401s, confirm starter helper sets Authorization explicitly or upgrade sdk-edge."
evan: will open a small hotfix PR to the published starter with the defensive helper and README note.
priya: filing an internal bug to align retry behavior between sdk-js and sdk-edge so we can remove the workaround later.
